{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792943577,"nonce":"pjYtSpMVVRldYs0mUA9KHORNgw0=","message":"Findings 2026-10-25, from the rayzor and ashui sessions.\n\nrayzor-34: no wasm frontend work is in progress; the plan is acceptable. `git grep rayzor_runtime:: compiler/src/ir` is 22 uses in 13 files and every one is a constant or type, not a call: `type_system::{ValueTag, TYPE_DYNAMIC_TOKEN, TYPE_CLASS_TOKEN, TYPE_ENUM_TOKEN, TYPE_FROM_HEADER, TYPE_USER_START, TYPE_BOOL/FLOAT/INT/STRING, NULL_INT}` and `haxe_array::HAXE_ARRAY_BOXED_ELEMS`. Moving those into rayzor-runtime-core removes the runtime dependency from the lowering. Also: cranelift_backend and tiered_backend are not behind a feature and must be gated for a `frontend` feature; blade compression on wasm should be ruzstd, decode-only (same zstd format as native); a file-provider trait in the lsp crate is fine, but caribou git-bug 19f542ae (rayzor-lsp as a library, module provider) is planning a seam too, so the two must be agreed first. runtime-wasm shares nothing with the frontend.\n\nashui-4e: tested in a page: the dashboard app (Css engine with compiled stylesheet, canvases, 3D, gestures, audio, SVG icons, embedded fonts), IME/clipboard/cursor agent in xwindow. NOT tested in a page: CodeEditor, text input with IME end to end, TopLayer popups, Dialog, Select. Page memory: dashboard uses 614 MB of the 1 GiB shared-memory ceiling (512 MB reserved before main; `?env=ASH_GC_HEAP_MB=400` bounds the heap). Dashboard wasm is 23.0 MB (5.5 MB brotli), 3,095 Haxe functions = 9.9 MB, lowered at build time by `ash --build`; ready in 12.8 s at 10 Mbit/s and 4.9 s at 50 Mbit/s with brotli. No filesystem in the page, no socket or fetch exposed: a WebSocket would be a new page agent like xavi/hlavi's fetch (ask ash-7d). Relevant open ashui issues: 56695d7 (files at run time) and 54e0e0e (a 4 to 5 s whole-loop stall near the heap ceiling, which a long-lived RayDE page could meet). Harness to copy: ashui tests/wasm/ (lib.sh, smoke.sh, run.sh, run_page.mjs), apps/dashboard as the template, ashui.macro.WebPage.\n\nNext: a minimal CodeEditor page in the web lane, `ash --build` of rayde.hl to get its size, and the Workspace provider seam in RayDE.","files":null}]}